1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,035
Every app about shared money asks one person to go first.

2
00:00:04,035 --> 00:00:08,971
Ours asks two people the same six open questions, each answering
alone.

3
00:00:08,971 --> 00:00:11,653
Neither of you ever sees what the other wrote.

4
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:16,260
That is only worth doing if the answer is measured rather than
guessed.

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:23,018
So every sentence on the page has to clear a number the model
returned, and there are controls that have to stay silent.

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:26,928
Maya gets a code to hand over, and then six questions.

7
00:00:26,928 --> 00:00:28,582
What does money feel like to her.

8
00:00:28,582 --> 00:00:30,730
Whether he notices what things cost.

9
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:33,073
Whether she has ever said so out loud.

10
00:00:33,649 --> 00:00:36,515
Before she seals them, she sees the hash.

11
00:00:36,515 --> 00:00:41,751
So she can check that what arrived is what she sent, and that nobody
quietly rewrote it.

12
00:00:42,329 --> 00:00:43,100
Sealed.

13
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,350
It is with him now.

14
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:48,582
And because the page is built from both of them, it does not exist
yet.

15
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:50,066
There is nothing to look at.

16
00:00:50,629 --> 00:00:52,219
Sam answers the same way.

17
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:57,440
And now the page exists, for both of them, at once, saying the same
thing.

18
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,368
You are both carrying it alone.

19
00:00:59,368 --> 00:01:01,750
Neither of you had ever said that out loud.

20
00:01:03,319 --> 00:01:04,688
And it is not a script.

21
00:01:04,688 --> 00:01:11,316
Change one of her six answers, and the finding that depended on it is
withheld, while the other two still stand.

22
00:01:14,279 --> 00:01:17,887
Nobody goes first, so nobody can be wrong first.

23
00:01:17,887 --> 00:01:20,244
Ours is live and open source.

